  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The search line for \(P = ax + by\) has gradient \(-a/b\). It leaves R at the vertex where its gradient lies between the gradients of the two edges that meet there. You can also work out \(P\) at each vertex.</p><p>\(P = {@obs[1][1]@}x + {@obs[1][2]@}y\): gradient \({@grs[1]@}\), greatest at {@ta[1]@}. \(P = {@obs[2][1]@}x + {@obs[2][2]@}y\): gradient \({@grs[2]@}\), greatest at {@ta[2]@}. \(P = {@obs[3][1]@}x + {@obs[3][2]@}y\): gradient \({@grs[3]@}\), greatest at {@ta[3]@}.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
